  "id": "Compound::DB00604 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Cisapride is linked to Cyp2d6 through a series of molecular interactions involving arachidonic acid metabolism. The evidence suggests that Cisapride binds to Cyp2a6, which then participates in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, a process catalyzed by arachidonic acid monooxygenase or epoxygenase activities. These activities are ultimately participated by Cyp2d6, indicating a potential role for Cyp2d6 in the metabolic pathway of arachidonic acid. The shared involvement of Cyp2d6 in arachidonic acid metabolism across different isoforms (Cyp2a6 and Cyp2c8) highlights a conserved mechanism, suggesting that Cyp2d6 may be a key player in the enzymatic conversion of arachidonic acid. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, biologically plausible relationship, though the exact functional role of Cyp2d6 in this context remains to be fully elucidated.",
